From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:43:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_hqdn3d_opencl: add an OpenCL hqdn3d filter

Add hqdn3d_opencl, an OpenCL port of the integer hqdn3d filter whose
output is identical to the CPU filter. It takes the options and
commands of hqdn3d and uses the shared tables in hqdn3d_coefs.c.

A horizontal kernel filters each row into an intermediate buffer; a
vertical kernel filters each column and applies the temporal lowpass
against the previous output. The temporal state is dropped where
hqdn3d drops it, and after a frame size change inside a running graph
the output frames come from a frames context of the new size.

The OpenCL frames context has no LSB-aligned 10- or 12-bit planar
format, so the high-depth planar formats are the 16-bit ones; p010,
p012 and p016 are accepted.

tools/hqdn3d_reset_test now also runs the OpenCL filter with an
ocl:<platform>.<device> argument.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
